# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000360  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to automatically create trouble
# tickets for organization-defined threats and events of interest as they
# are detected in real time (within seconds).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000360
group:           V-206515
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    Splunk can hand a triggered detection to an outside system as it fires,
                 through the webhook alert action or a script action, which is how a ticket
                 is opened from the application without a person in the loop.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<saved search>] action.webhook in 1|true and savedsearches.conf [<saved search>] action.webhook.param.url non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [] enableSched equals 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [webhook] command present -> savedsearches.conf [<saved search>] action.webhook in 1|true and savedsearches.conf [<saved search>] action.webhook.param.url non_empty
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [webhook] command https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The ticket system itself and the endpoint it accepts submissions on, which
                 the application posts to but does not provide.
external:        Which threats and events of interest warrant a ticket, left to the
                 organization by the check text.
external:        Detection "within seconds" depends on a real-time or continuously
                 scheduled search and the search capacity to sustain it, which is a sizing
                 and deployment-design decision rather than a setting.
external:        Where the server performs no analysis, the benchmark marks the requirement
                 not applicable, which is a deployment-design determination.

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-AU-000360 check text;
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:599 ([webhook]), alert_actions.conf.spec:87
                 (command), alert_actions.conf.spec:100 (payload_format = [xml|json],
                 default xml), savedsearches.conf.spec:73 (enableSched),
                 savedsearches.conf.spec:403 (action.script)
finding:         No alert action is configured that can hand a triggered detection to an
                 outside system, or detections are not scheduled to run by themselves, so
                 the application cannot open a ticket as an event of interest is detected.
